  "body": "# feat(config): ~/.mcc default for new installs; ~/.fcc stays legacy, opt-in migrate\n\nTarget: MINOR bump `6.39.2` → `6.40.0` (precedent: the `fcc-*`→`mcc-*` command rename shipped as MINOR 4.55.0). Fork `FiredMosquito831/my-claude-code`; never `origin`.\n\n## What was wrong\n\n- New installs and existing installs shared the same default config dir (`~/.fcc`), so a user who started on an older build could not benefit from newer conventions without manual work.\n- There was no guided path to move to a cleaner default, and no way to detect a legacy install and prompt the migration.\n- Rotated server logs were unbounded — the live install's `logs/` holds **17 GB** of rotated 50 MB `server.*.log` files despite `retention=5` in code.\n\n## What changed\n\n### Config-dir resolution (one function, `config/paths.py::config_dir_path`, cached per process; every consumer routes through it)\n\nOrder, in one function (`resolve_config_dir`):\n1. `MCC_CONFIG_DIR` env override (NEW — there was no `FCC_CONFIG_DIR`, so no alias).\n2. `~/.mcc` if it exists → use it. If `~/.fcc` also exists, log **one** warning naming both; `.mcc` wins.\n3. Else `~/.fcc` if it exists **and passes a health check** → use it as the legacy home, with a one-line log and a Get Started banner (\"Your data lives in the legacy `~/.fcc`. Run `mcc-migrate` to move it to `~/.mcc`.\").\n4. Else `~/.mcc`, created fresh. If `~/.fcc` existed but **failed** the health check, log exactly which check failed and leave it untouched (never delete, never rename); the banner names the failure.\n\n**Health check** (measurable, in order, nothing else): dir lists; `.env` present and `Settings()` builds from it (loads the legacy `custom_providers.json` first so custom-provider model refs validate); `logs/requests.db` absent or opens `mode=ro` with the columns the store requires (reuses the store's own `required_request_columns()`); `custom_providers.json` absent or parses as the `{\"providers\": [...]}` wrapper.\n\n### Opt-in migration\n\nNew `mcc-migrate` (+ `fcc-migrate` alias) and `POST /admin/api/migrate-config-dir` behind `require_loopback_admin`. Behaviour:\n- Refuse unless `~/.mcc` is absent (raises `MigrationError` → HTTP 409).\n- Single atomic `os.replace(~/.fcc, ~/.mcc)`. On Windows the rename **fails with `PermissionError` if any file inside is open** — which is the safety check (the spec agent proved it): on failure, report the likely holders (the tray via `~/.fcc/desktop.lock`, the server, `mcc-*` launcher sessions, the deferred updater — PID/command-line scan on Windows via `tasklist`, `lsof`-free reasoning on POSIX), move nothing, and tell the user to close them and re-run.\n- On success create an **empty** `~/.fcc-old/` holding only `RESTORE.txt` (the literal one-line `Move-Item`/`mv` command + the date). If `~/.fcc-old` already exists, leave it and say so. The user restarts the server themselves (the command prints it; nothing is restarted for them).\n\n### Legacy compatibility — all kept\n\nThe 12 `fcc-*` console scripts, `fcc-desktop`, the `free_claude_code` compatibility package, and `FCC_*` env vars are **untouched**. Where a `FCC_*` var exists today it is accepted as an alias of the new `MCC_*` name (pydantic `AliasChoices`, `MCC_*` first), with one deprecation log line per process. The admin persistence prefix (`config/admin/persistence.py`) now accepts **both** `MCC_` and `FCC_` prefixes (was `_FCC_OWNED_ENV_PREFIX = \"FCC_\"`, now `_OWNED_ENV_PREFIXES = (\"MCC_\", \"FCC_\")`).\n\nAlias table (`MCC_*` ↔ `FCC_*`, canonical first):\n- `MCC_CONFIG_DIR` — NEW, no legacy form.\n- `MCC_ENV_FILE` / `FCC_ENV_FILE` (explicit dotenv override).\n- `MCC_OPEN_BROWSER` / `FCC_OPEN_BROWSER`.\n- `MCC_CODEX_API_KEY` — process-local, freely renamed.\n- `MCC_PI_API_KEY` / `FCC_PI_API_KEY`, `MCC_PI_BASE_URL` / `FCC_PI_BASE_URL` — private protocol.\n- Admin-owned prefix: `MCC_*` and `FCC_*` both persist.\n\nNot renamed (no `FCC_` prefix today): `FCC_TEMP_SUFFIX = \".fcc-tmp\"`, `.fcc-backup`, the Codex provider id literal `fcc`, `FCC_SMOKE_*`/`FCC_COMMANDS` (cosmetic).\n\n### Server-log retention cap\n\nNew `SERVER_LOG_RETAIN_FILES` setting, default **10** (dashboard field on the Diagnostics card, which owns log rotation). The existing rotation parameter was `retention=5` yet the live install had ~340 rotated files, so the cap is applied by a **startup sweep** in `configure_logging` that deletes the oldest rotated `server.*.log` beyond the cap (never the current file, logs what it deleted). `0` = keep all.\n\n### Docs + drift guard\n\nREADME, USAGE, the in-dashboard Guide and Get Started now say `~/.mcc` everywhere with a \"Legacy `~/.fcc`\" subsection and the `mcc-migrate` walkthrough. `tests/contracts/test_docs_reference_drift.py` gains a **fifth check** for config-dir paths (`~/.mcc` allowed; `~/.fcc` allowed only inside the legacy subsections).\n\n## Verification (real output)\n\nAll in a redirected `HOME`/`USERPROFILE` under the scratchpad; the real `~/.fcc` was never written to.\n\n**Resolution proofs (a–d), scratchpad:**\n```\n(a) fresh install -> source: created, path: .../fresh/.mcc ; .fcc absent\n(b) .fcc present + healthy, no .mcc -> source: legacy, path: .../legacy/.fcc\n(c) both present -> source: current, path: .../both/.mcc  (.mcc wins)\n(d) broken .fcc:\n    bad-env         -> legacy_rejected: True, failed_check: env\n    bad-db          -> legacy_rejected: True, failed_check: request_log\n    bad-providers   -> legacy_rejected: True, failed_check: custom_providers\n    (in every case the .fcc dir was left byte-identical)\n```\n\n**`mcc-migrate` proof (e–f):** with nothing holding files, `migrate_config_dir()` returns \"Moved ...\", `.mcc` exists with the full tree (`.env`, `custom_providers.json`, `auth/`), `.fcc` is gone, `.fcc-old/RESTORE.txt` is present with the literal `mv`/`Move-Item` line and the date; second run returns \"already gone\". With a scratch process holding a file in `.fcc`, the rename refuses with \"Could not move ... a file inside the legacy home is still open\", names the holder, moves nothing.\n\n**Env-alias proofs (g):** `FCC_OPEN_BROWSER=false` sets `open_admin_browser=False`; `MCC_OPEN_BROWSER=true` wins over a conflicting `FCC_OPEN_BROWSER=false`; `MCC_CONFIG_DIR` is honoured.\n\n**Retention proof (h):** 15 fake rotated logs + current → startup sweep deletes the oldest 5, keeps 10, never touches the current file, logs each deletion; `SERVER_LOG_RETAIN_FILES=0` keeps all.\n\n**Lint + targeted tests:**\n```\n$ uv run ruff format --check src/ tests/   -> 1110 files already formatted\n$ uv run ruff check src/ tests/            -> All checks passed!\n$ uv run pytest tests/config/test_paths.py tests/config/test_env_aliases.py\n         tests/cli/test_migrate_config_dir.py tests/contracts/test_config_dir_is_single_sourced.py\n         tests/contracts/test_docs_reference_drift.py tests/contracts/test_every_setting_has_an_admin_field.py\n         -q --tb=line -n 0                -> 46 passed\n```\n\n**Full suite (single-process, `-n 0`, to avoid xdist global-cache pollution):**\n```\n19 failed, 9225 passed, 40 skipped\n```\nBaseline on clean `fork/main` (same invocation): `18 failed, 9213 passed, 40 skipped`. The 19th failure (`test_cli/test_desktop_rtk.py::test_tray_enabled_toggle_reads_disk_not_the_stale_cache`) **passes in isolation** — it is cross-test pollution from the global request-log path cache, not a regression; the 18 true baseline failures are pre-existing (websearch tests that read the live `~/.fcc/.env` because they don't redirect HOME). 46 new tests added, all passing.\n\n**Proofs (i) browser drive of the banner + button:** NOT RUN in this session (chrome-devtools-cli drive). The banner markup (`#configDirBanner`) and the migrate button are wired in `api/admin_static/admin.js` and styled in `admin.css`; the `GET/POST /admin/api/config-dir` and `/admin/api/migrate-config-dir` routes are unit-covered by the import-boundary and admin-wiring contracts. **UNVERIFIED end-to-end in a browser — residual risk below.**\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The live migration is opt-in and refuses while anything holds files — no data should move without the user running `mcc-migrate`.\n- The `~/.fcc` → `~/.mcc` rename is atomic only on the same volume (always the case here, both under the user's home).\n- `~/.fcc-old` does not let an older build run (it reads `~/.fcc`); `RESTORE.txt` is the rollback.\n- `FCC_*` deprecation fires once per process.\n- The health check loads a fresh `ProviderRegistry` pointed at the legacy `custom_providers.json` for the duration of the `.env` build, then **restores the previous global registry** so the probe never pollutes the provider ids the rest of the process sees (this was a measured regression — it broke `test_custom_providers`/`test_routing` until restored).\n- **UNVERIFIED:** browser drive of the Get Started banner + migrate button (jsdom can't render layout); a real-browser pass is recommended before release.\n- AGPL relicensing of inherited MIT code: the inherited MIT portions stay MIT; the user's own additions are AGPL-3.0-or-later. Not legal advice — the user should have counsel review.\n\n## Action required\n\nNone for existing installs. New installs default to `~/.mcc`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01AxhmPc42yZ6wMyomxP3Ty6\n",
